#  Basura de herramienta, no del diseno. Todo lo demas se sube tal cual,
#  artefactos generados incluidos.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ext/

#  Documents, and the scripts whose only job is to make them. These are the
#  team's own working material and are shared through another channel; the
#  repository is the DESIGN. Knowledge documents -- HANDOFF.md, the READMEs --
#  do go up: they are what lets someone pick the flow back up.
*.pdf
hacer_pdf*
documento.py
figuras*.py
graficas.py
capturar*.py

#  Documentation lives in Juander28/GDS_GENERATOR, together with the
#  generator it documents. Keeping it out of here keeps the design repository
#  to the design: schematics, layouts, netlists, GDS.
*.md

#  The submission interface lives at the REPOSITORY ROOT, and only there.
#  The chipathon's external LVS reads ./info.yaml -> project.lvs_config ->
#  ./lvs_config.json; the copies that used to sit here came along with the
#  working tree and were a second source of truth that silently drifted --
#  the root pair once named B26_A_filled.gds while these named _filled3, and
#  the root one is the one that counts. Keep them out so a `cp -a` of the
#  working tree cannot reintroduce them.
info.yaml
lvs_config.json
